      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Independent synthesis: in a glovebox, SmI3(THF)3 (500 mg, 0.66 mmol) was dissolved in 10 mL of N-MeIm. The color changed slowly from yellow to pale yellow. After 20 min the solvent was removed under high vacuum (10^-5 Torr) and the residue was washed with THF to give 5 as a pale bronze powder (755 mg, 95%). Crystals of 5 (benzene solvate) were also obtained by diffusion of benzene into a solution of 1 in N-MeIm (7-10 days), giving pale yellow crystals that were hand-separated from 6. In the crystal, eight N-MeIm ligands form a square antiprism about Sm(III); iodides are noncoordinating.",
