        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Diffusion of benzene into a solution of divalent 1 in N-MeIm in a glovebox over 7-10 days reproducibly gave a mixture of THF-insoluble crystals that were separated by hand: pale yellow 5 and colorless 6, formed by hydrolysis. 6 contains a triangle of Sm(N-MeIm)4 units bridged by three in-plane μ-OH ligands and two μ3-OH ligands; four iodide counterions do not bind Sm. Attempts to crystallize 1 from THF at ambient temperature over 2 days gave a THF-insoluble colorless material analyzing as 6 less one N-MeIm per samarium. Crystal lattice includes two N-MeIm, 2.5 benzene, and one THF.",
