        "procedure": "Compound 5 is very soluble in N-MeIm; crystallization over long periods leads to hydroxide complex 7. Diffusion of benzene into a solution of 5 in N-MeIm in a glovebox over 2 months gave THF-insoluble colorless crystals of 7. The dimeric tetracation contains seven-coordinate samarium centers: two Sm(N-MeIm)5 units bridged by two μ-OH ligands; iodides are noncoordinating. The dimer sits on a twofold axis with a benzene solvent molecule.",
